{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, just logging in, this thing's crawling. Take a seat. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Burning when I wee. Again. I'm over it.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the screen froze. Sarah, you're thirty-eight, burning when you wee?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Third time this year.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, maybe the fourth. I lose count.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She's been miserable with that burning. It started about a week ago.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): The burning did not start a week ago. Two days. Let me talk, Karen.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right, so somewhere between two days and a week. You're Karen, her sister?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yeah, I'm Karen. I drove her. She was up all night on the loo.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Not all night. I got up twice. I'm just wrecked, that's all.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Twice. Okay. Any blood in the wee?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Pain up in your back, over the kidneys?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. It's just the stinging, and I'm going all the time.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): How often is all the time?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): About every hour. During the day. It's annoying.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fever, or feeling shivery?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever. I'm just tired and cranky.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say the fever bit again, I clicked the wrong tab.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): I said no. No fever.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): And down below, any vaginal discharge or itch?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing like that. Can we not.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She gets embarrassed. She also pinched some of my tablets.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): They were your leftover antibiotics, not your hair vitamins. I didn't touch the biotin.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hang on, whose biotin?",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Mine. Biotin for my hair. And her husband Dave's on metformin for his sugar, but she doesn't take that either.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay, ignore those. What antibiotic did you actually take?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Karen's leftover trimethoprim, for the burning. I swallowed one at night for two nights, then the packet was empty.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): What dose? Say that again, the cursor jumped.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Trimethoprim, one at night for two nights. The bottle said 300, I think, maybe. I don't really know.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): So you stopped when they ran out. Any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): No. None.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): The vaginal symptoms, I'll ask once more. Discharge or itch?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Ugh, fine. There's a bit of an itch, and no discharge. Happy?",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): A bit of itch, no discharge. Noted. Still stinging today?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes. Right now. It's worse when I actually pee.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She barely drinks water. Lives on coffee at work.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): I drink water. Not enough, maybe. I'm a receptionist, stuck at a desk.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): This is probably another bout of cystitis, with the burning and how often you're going.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Great.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll send a urine off for microscopy and culture today. We won't start another antibiotic until that comes back.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): So I just sit with it?",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): Push the fluids, plain water, and please don't take anyone else's tablets again.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I told her that.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): If it hasn't settled in three days, or if you get a fever or back pain, come straight back. Otherwise we'll ring you about the result.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Three days. Fine. Can we go?",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yeah. Grab a jar from the desk on the way out, midstream if you can.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): I know how a wee sample works."
 ],
